  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 158 AM MDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nHigh pressure overhead continues to mean warming temperatures and \ndry conditions across our coverage area. While morning temperatures \nwill generally be in the 30s for the next few mornings, highs return \nto the 60s each afternoon, pushing towards near 70 degrees around \nthe Burley area by Saturday afternoon, with temperatures just a \ncouple of degrees cooler on Sunday. Overall, it should be a very \npleasant end of the week/weekend for anyone with outdoor plans or if \nyou are just looking forward to having the windows open!\n\nAn upper level low drops south along the West Coast early next week \nand will eventually bring us cooler temperatures and wetter \nconditions. Now, WHEN the precipitation actually arrives is a bit of \na toss up at this point. The ECMWF brings some precipitation chances \nfrom this low to our area as early as Tuesday morning and then more \non Thursday/Friday. The GFS does bring some light precipitation on \nTuesday, but it really holds off on the main push of precipitation \nuntil almost Friday. We'll see how far south this low actually drops \nand how quickly it moves eastward and how models continue to change \nover the next few days. At this point, the NBM brings temperatures \nback down to the 50s as early as Tuesday and 30 to 40 percent \nprecipitation chances to most of our area almost every day next week \nafter Monday.",
